00:02:36,420 --> 00:02:40,420
something, I'll do it well. And I'll also know where things are and how to access them and make

28
00:02:40,420 --> 00:02:47,480
use of them because I've done some compensatory things or someone has. So with sapphires, we tend

29
00:02:47,480 --> 00:02:52,180
to sustain our awareness skills, although sometimes it's tough for us to think things through and

30
00:02:52,180 --> 00:02:57,140
things still surprise us. With diamonds, when you're in a diamond state, your old emotions

31
00:02:57,140 --> 00:02:59,480
and your old abilities sort of change. And so I think it's important to know where you're

32
00:02:59,500 --> 00:03:26,960
going. And so I'm going to go back to the

33
00:03:26,960 --> 00:03:30,240
Aware of the situation from the external point of view.

34
00:03:31,060 --> 00:03:32,920
Rubies, only in moments.

35
00:03:33,040 --> 00:03:34,460
I'm a lot less body aware.

36
00:03:34,800 --> 00:03:38,020
And so my skill sets, my fine motor skills,

37
00:03:38,260 --> 00:03:41,240
I may not know what I don't know,

38
00:03:41,340 --> 00:03:44,680
or I may, and I may come and seek assistance.

39
00:03:45,020 --> 00:03:46,100
So it varies.

40
00:03:47,060 --> 00:03:49,780
And pearls, I tend to be more inside aware

41
00:03:49,780 --> 00:03:50,760
than outside aware.

42
00:03:50,760 --> 00:03:54,100
So situation-wise, I don't know I'm hungry

43
00:03:54,100 --> 00:03:55,840
and I'm actually not feeling that.

44
00:03:55,920 --> 00:03:56,900
I'm not thirsty.

45
00:03:57,040 --> 00:03:59,620
Or maybe I am, and I don't know how to communicate it.

46
00:04:00,400 --> 00:04:02,440
So situation varies.

47
00:04:03,040 --> 00:04:04,940
Now let's talk about safety.

48
00:04:05,280 --> 00:04:07,920
Well, the problem is with safety, it all depends.

49
00:04:08,840 --> 00:04:11,160
So that's the one people tend to think about.

50
00:04:11,340 --> 00:04:13,720
So here's the quick version for me.

51
00:04:14,240 --> 00:04:16,520
Sapphires, if you have it, you use it.

52
00:04:16,580 --> 00:04:18,080
So you sustain whatever you've got.

53
00:04:18,140 --> 00:04:19,060
You want to keep it going.

54
00:04:19,060 --> 00:04:20,440
But if you're safe, you're safe.

55
00:04:20,560 --> 00:04:22,460
If you're not, you never have been.

56
00:04:22,680 --> 00:04:23,820
And you've had lots of accidents.

57
00:04:24,500 --> 00:04:26,940
Diamonds, typically you need a second set of eyes.

58
00:04:27,040 --> 00:04:30,380
Because about 50% of the time, you may be inaccurate

59
00:04:30,380 --> 00:04:32,400
related to the skills you have in that moment.

60
00:04:33,280 --> 00:04:36,880
Emeralds, probably benefit from a friendly preset.

61
00:04:37,160 --> 00:04:39,300
Prompts, reduce the risk.

62
00:04:39,760 --> 00:04:40,760
Check out mistakes.

63
00:04:41,380 --> 00:04:42,520
Modify in the moment.

64
00:04:42,760 --> 00:04:43,920
So you need somebody around.

65
00:04:44,040 --> 00:04:45,480
Not interfering, but present.

66
00:04:46,360 --> 00:04:50,260
Ambers, 24-7 you need somebody to sort of watch the environment,

67
00:04:50,440 --> 00:04:52,320
watch the task, keep an eye on the person

68
00:04:52,320 --> 00:04:56,300
to make sure what is happening is safe for the individual

69
00:04:56,300 --> 00:04:56,940
and makes sense.

70
00:04:57,080 --> 00:04:58,620
Does that make sense for the individual?

71
00:04:58,620 --> 00:05:00,940
Because in that moment, it's just a moment.

72
00:05:01,180 --> 00:05:03,100
And be able to back up and try again.

73
00:05:03,320 --> 00:05:07,080
Rubies, eyes on with an arm's reach pretty much all the time

74
00:05:07,080 --> 00:05:10,660
because of the variation in ability and inability.

75
00:05:10,860 --> 00:05:14,500
And pearls, we need somebody in immediate space 24-7.

76
00:05:14,700 --> 00:05:16,300
So that's safety monitoring.

77
00:05:16,500 --> 00:05:18,800
Doesn't mean you interfere, but it means you're present

78
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:22,280
and accounted for and you're present in every sense.

79
00:05:22,480 --> 00:05:24,120
Then we get to access.

80
00:05:24,320 --> 00:05:26,020
Well, how accessible are things?

81
00:05:26,020 --> 00:05:27,780
How can people get to them?

82
00:05:27,980 --> 00:05:30,340
With sapphires, you can actually consider hidden access.

83
00:05:30,540 --> 00:05:33,300
You sort of know where you keep things or where things can be put

84
00:05:33,500 --> 00:05:36,900
or the person that you're living with, not just for yourself.

85
00:05:37,100 --> 00:05:37,820
So you know where they are,

86
00:05:38,020 --> 00:05:42,020
but they can't get to them unless you want that to happen.

87
00:05:42,220 --> 00:05:45,820
Diamonds, we may have emergency controls when monitoring is impossible

88
00:05:46,020 --> 00:05:49,020
and the person has varying awareness.

89
00:05:49,220 --> 00:05:53,300
Emeralds, we probably need to control over access unless we're monitoring

90
00:05:53,500 --> 00:05:54,500
during critical pieces.

91
00:05:54,700 --> 00:05:55,960
You can't just turn people loose.

92
00:05:56,160 --> 00:05:59,340
They can't do that because they possibly could, but they very possibly couldn't.

93
00:05:59,540 --> 00:06:01,500
And they may or may not know that.

94
00:06:01,700 --> 00:06:05,700
Ambers, we want to control what we want people to have access to.

95
00:06:05,900 --> 00:06:09,460
But we also have to offer what they do like to do.

96
00:06:09,660 --> 00:06:13,860
And then rubies, supported access or no access.

97
00:06:14,060 --> 00:06:16,660
But we've got to manage the environment and access.

98
00:06:16,860 --> 00:06:23,380
Access to steps, access to outdoors, access to hot, to cold, to food, to drink.

99
00:06:23,580 --> 00:06:24,980
Everything has to be managed.

100
00:06:25,080 --> 00:06:26,540
And it's a big job.

101
00:06:26,740 --> 00:06:29,740
And then with pearls, we need supported provision.

102
00:06:29,940 --> 00:06:33,300
And if we don't give them access, we have to be the access.

103
00:06:33,500 --> 00:06:35,180
And so things are changing yet again.

104
00:06:35,380 --> 00:06:37,300
Just when you thought, well, it doesn't matter.

105
00:06:37,500 --> 00:06:40,180
Yeah, it does, because if we don't provide it, it doesn't happen.

106
00:06:40,380 --> 00:06:42,540
When do I get to go outside and feel the sun?

107
00:06:42,740 --> 00:06:45,340
When do I get to sit under a tree?

108
00:06:45,540 --> 00:06:49,060
